H7800.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7799;
Meaning: Shushan, a place in Persia
KJV renders: Shushan.

H7801.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) of foreign origin;
Meaning: a Shushankite (collectively) or inhabitants of some unknown place in Assyrian
KJV renders: Susanchites.

H7802.strongs:
Origin: or (plural of former) שׁוֹשַׁנִּים עֵדוּתlemma שׁוֹשַׁנִּיס עֵדוּת samekh, corrected to שׁוֹשַׁנִּים עֵדוּת; from 7799 and 5715; lily (or trumpet) of assemblage;
Meaning: Shushan-Eduth or Shoshannim-Eduth, the title of a popular song
KJV renders: Shoshannim-Eduth, Shushan-eduth.

H7803.strongs:
Origin: probably from 7582 and the same as 8520; crash of breakage;
Meaning: Shuthelach, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Shuthelah.

H7804.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 5800;
Meaning: to leave, i.e. (causatively) free
KJV renders: deliver.

H7805.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tan (by sunburning); figuratively (as if by a piercing ray) to scan
KJV renders: look up, see.

H7806.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to twist (a thread of straw)
KJV renders: twine.

H7807.strongs:
Origin: from 7817;
Meaning: sunk, i.e. downcast
KJV renders: humble.

H7808.strongs:
Origin: for 7879;
Meaning: communion, i.e. (reflexively) meditation
KJV renders: thought.

H7809.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to donate, i.e. bribe
KJV renders: hire, give a reward.

H7810.strongs:
Origin: from 7809;
Meaning: a donation (venal or redemptive)
KJV renders: bribe(-ry), gift, present, reward.

H7811.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to swim; causatively, to inundate
KJV renders: (make to) swim.

H7812.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to depress, i.e. prostrate (especially reflexive, in homage to royalty or God)
KJV renders: bow (self) down, crouch, fall down (flat), humbly beseech, do (make) obeisance, do reverence, make to stoop, worship.

H7813.strongs:
Origin: from 7811;
Meaning: a pond (for swimming)
KJV renders: to swim in.

H7814.strongs:
Origin: or שְׂחֹק; from 7832;
Meaning: laughter (in merriment or defiance)
KJV renders: derision, laughter(-ed to scorn, -ing), mocked, sport.

H7815.strongs:
Origin: from 7835;
Meaning: dinginess, i.e. perhaps soot
KJV renders: coal.

H7816.strongs:
Origin: from 7812;
Meaning: pit
KJV renders: pit.

H7817.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to sink or depress (reflexive or causative)
KJV renders: bend, bow (down), bring (cast) down, couch, humble self, be (bring) low, stoop.

H7818.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tread out, i.e. squeeze (grapes)
KJV renders: press.

H7819.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)
KJV renders: kill, offer, shoot out, slay, slaughter.

H7820.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with 7819 through the idea of striking);
Meaning: to hammer out
KJV renders: beat.

H7821.strongs:
Origin: from 7819;
Meaning: slaughter
KJV renders: killing.

H7822.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to burn;
Meaning: inflammation, i.e. an ulcer
KJV renders: boil, botch.

H7823.strongs:
Origin: or סָחִישׁ; from an unused root apparently meaning to sprout;
Meaning: after-growth
KJV renders: (that) which springeth of the same.

H7824.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7828;
Meaning: a board (as chipped thin)
KJV renders: cieled with.

H7825.strongs:
Origin: from 7812;
Meaning: a pit-fall (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: destruction, pit.

H7826.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to roar;
Meaning: a lion (from his characteristic roar)
KJV renders: (fierce) lion.

H7827.strongs:
Origin: apparently from the same as 7826 through some obscure idea, perhaps that of peeling off by concussion of sound;
Meaning: a scale or shell, i.e. the aromatic mussel.
KJV renders: onycha.

H7828.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to peel, i.e. emaciate;
Meaning: the gull (as thin)
KJV renders: cuckoo.

H7829.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7828;
Meaning: emaciation
KJV renders: consumption.

H7830.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root apparently meaning to strut;
Meaning: haughtiness (as evinced by the attitude)
KJV renders: × lion, pride.

H7831.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7830; proudly;
Meaning: Shachatsom, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shahazimah (from the margin).

H7832.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to laugh (in pleasure or detraction); by implication, to play
KJV renders: deride, have in derision, laugh, make merry, mock(-er), play, rejoice, (laugh to) scorn, be in (make) sport.

H7833.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to comminate (by trituration or attrition)
KJV renders: beat, wear.

H7834.strongs:
Origin: from 7833;
Meaning: a powder (as beaten small); by analogy, a thin vapor; by extension, the firmament
KJV renders: cloud, small dust, heaven, sky.

H7835.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with 7836 through the idea of the duskiness of early dawn);
Meaning: to be dim or dark (in color)
KJV renders: be black.

H7836.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to dawn, i.e. (figuratively) be (up) early at any task (with the implication of earnestness); by extension, to search for (with painstaking)
KJV renders: (do something) betimes, enquire early, rise (seek) betimes, seek diligently) early, in the morning).

H7837.strongs:
Origin: from 7836;
Meaning: dawn (literal, figurative or adverbial)
KJV renders: day(-spring), early, light, morning, whence riseth.

H7838.strongs:
Origin: or שָׁחוֹר; from 7835;
Meaning: properly, dusky, but also (absol.) jetty
KJV renders: black.

H7839.strongs:
Origin: from 7836;
Meaning: a dawning, i.e. (figuratively) juvenescence
KJV renders: youth.

H7840.strongs:
Origin: from 7835;
Meaning: swarthy
KJV renders: black.

H7841.strongs:
Origin: from 7836 and 3050; Jah has sought;
Meaning: Shecharjah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shehariah.

H7842.strongs:
Origin: dual of 7837; double dawn;
Meaning: Shacharajim, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shaharaim.

H7843.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: batter, cast off, corrupt(-er, thing), destroy(-er, -uction), lose, mar, perish, spill, spoiler, × utterly, waste(-r).

H7845.strongs:
Origin: from 7743;
Meaning: a pit (especially as a trap); figuratively, destruction
KJV renders: corruption, destruction, ditch, grave, pit.

H7846.strongs:
Origin: or סֵט; from 7750;
Meaning: a departure from right, i.e. sin
KJV renders: revolter, that turn aside.

H7847.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to deviate from duty
KJV renders: decline, go aside, turn.

H7848.strongs:
Origin: feminine of a derivative (only in the plural שִׁטִּים; meaning the sticks of wood) from the same as 7850;
Meaning: the acacia (from its scourging thorns)
KJV renders: shittah, shittim. See also 1029.

H7849.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to expand
KJV renders: all abroad, enlarge, spread, stretch out.

H7851.strongs:
Origin: the same as the plural of 7848; acacia trees;
Meaning: Shittim, a place East of the Jordan
KJV renders: Shittim.

H7852.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to lurk for, i.e. persecute
KJV renders: hate, oppose self against.

H7853.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to attack, (figuratively) accuse
KJV renders: (be an) adversary, resist.

H7854.strongs:
Origin: from 7853;
Meaning: an opponent; especially (with the article prefixed) Satan, the arch-enemy of good
KJV renders: adversary, Satan, withstand.

H7855.strongs:
Origin: from 7853;
Meaning: opposition (by letter)
KJV renders: accusation.

H7856.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7855;
Meaning: Sitnah, the name of a well in Pal
KJV renders: Sitnah.

H7857.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to gush; by implication, to inundate, cleanse; by analogy, to gallop, conquer
KJV renders: drown, (over-) flow(-whelm, rinse, run, rush, (throughly) wash (away).

H7858.strongs:
Origin: or שֵׁטֶף; from 7857;
Meaning: a deluge (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: flood, outrageous, overflowing.

H7859.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: a side
KJV renders: side.

H7860.strongs:
Origin: active participle of an otherwise unused root probably meaning to write;
Meaning: properly, a scribe, i.e. (by analogy or implication) an official superintendent or magistrate
KJV renders: officer, overseer, ruler.

H7861.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7860; magisterial;
Meaning: Shitrai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shitrai.

H7862.strongs:
Origin: probably from 7737;
Meaning: a gift (as available)
KJV renders: present.

H7863.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7721 by permutation;
Meaning: elevation
KJV renders: excellency.

H7864.strongs:
Origin: for 7724;
Meaning: Sheja, an Israelite
KJV renders: Sheva (from the margin).

H7865.strongs:
Origin: from 7863; peak;
Meaning: Sion, the summit of Mount Hermon
KJV renders: Sion.

H7866.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7722; ruin;
Meaning: Shijon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shihon.

H7867.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to become aged, i.e. (by implication) to grow gray
KJV renders: (be) grayheaded.

H7869.strongs:
Origin: from 7867;
Meaning: old age
KJV renders: age.

H7870.strongs:
Origin: by permutation from 7725;
Meaning: a return (of property)
KJV renders: captivity.

H7871.strongs:
Origin: from 3427;
Meaning: residence
KJV renders: while...lay.

H7872.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 7869;
Meaning: old age
KJV renders: (be) gray (grey hoar,-y) hairs (head,-ed), old age.

H7873.strongs:
Origin: from 7734;
Meaning: a withdrawal (into a private place)
KJV renders: pursuing.

H7874.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root probably meaning to boil up (compare 7736); used only as denominative from 7875;
Meaning: to plaster
KJV renders: plaister.

H7875.strongs:
Origin: from 7874;
Meaning: lime (as boiling when slacked)
KJV renders: lime, plaister.

H7876.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to keep in memory
KJV renders: be unmindful. (Render Deuteronomy 32:18, 'A Rock bore thee, thou must recollect; and (yet) thou hast forgotten,' etc.)

H7877.strongs:
Origin: of unknown derivation;
Meaning: Shiza, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shiza.

H7878.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to ponder, i.e. (by implication) converse (with oneself, and hence, aloud) or (transitively) utter
KJV renders: commune, complain, declare, meditate, muse, pray, speak, talk (with).

H7879.strongs:
Origin: from 7878;
Meaning: a contemplation; by implication, an utterance
KJV renders: babbling, communication, complaint, meditation, prayer, talk.

H7880.strongs:
Origin: from 7878;
Meaning: a shoot (as if uttered or put forth), i.e. (generally) shrubbery
KJV renders: bush, plant, shrub.

H7881.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 7879;
Meaning: reflection; by extension, devotion
KJV renders: meditation, prayer.

H7882.strongs:
Origin: for 7745;
