KJV renders: pit.

H7883.strongs:
Origin: or שִׁחוֹר; or שִׁחֹר; probably from 7835; dark, i.e. turbid;
Meaning: Shichor, a stream of Egypt
KJV renders: Shihor, Sihor.

H7884.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7883 and 3835; darkish whiteness;
Meaning: Shichor-Libnath, a stream of Palestine
KJV renders: Shihor-libnath.

H7886.strongs:
Origin: from 7951; tranquil;
Meaning: Shiloh, an epithet of the Messiah
KJV renders: Shiloh.

H7887.strongs:
Origin: or שִׁלֹה; or שִׁילוֹ; or שִׁלוֹ; from the same as 7886;
Meaning: Shiloh, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shiloh.

H7888.strongs:
Origin: or שִׁילֹנִי; or שִׁלֹנִי; from 7887;
Meaning: a Shilonite or inhabitant of Shiloh
KJV renders: Shilonite.

H7889.strongs:
Origin: apparently for 3452; desert;
Meaning: Shimon, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shimon.

H7890.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to urinate;
Meaning: urine
KJV renders: piss.

H7891.strongs:
Origin: or (the original form) שׁוּר; (1 Samuel 18:6), a primitive root (rather identical with 7788 through the idea of strolling minstrelsy);
Meaning: to sing
KJV renders: behold (by mistake for 7789), sing(-er, -ing man, -ing woman).

H7892.strongs:
Origin: or feminine שִׁירָה; from 7891;
Meaning: a song; abstractly, singing
KJV renders: musical(-ick), × sing(-er, -ing), song.

H7894.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 7893; whiteness;
Meaning: Shisha, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shisha.

H7895.strongs:
Origin: or שׁוּשַׁק; of Egyptian derivation;
Meaning: Shishak, an Egyptian king
KJV renders: Shishak.

H7896.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to place (in a very wide application)
KJV renders: apply, appoint, array, bring, consider, lay (up), let alone, × look, make, mark, put (on), regard, set, shew, be stayed, × take.

H7897.strongs:
Origin: from 7896;
Meaning: a dress (as put on)
KJV renders: attire.

H7898.strongs:
Origin: from 7896;
Meaning: scrub or trash, i.e. wild growth of weeds or briers (as if put on the field)
KJV renders: thorns.

H7899.strongs:
Origin: from 5526 in the sense of 7753;
Meaning: a brier (as of a hedge)
KJV renders: prick.

H7900.strongs:
Origin: from 5526 in the sense of 7753;
Meaning: a booth (as interlaced)
KJV renders: tabernacle.

H7901.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to lie down (for rest, sexual connection, decease or any other purpose)
KJV renders: × at all, cast down, (lover-)lay (self) (down), (make to) lie (down, down to sleep, still with), lodge, ravish, take rest, sleep, stay.

H7902.strongs:
Origin: from 7901;
Meaning: a lying down (of dew, or for the sexual act)
KJV renders: × carnally, copulation, × lay, seed.

H7903.strongs:
Origin: from 7901;
Meaning: a (sexual) lying with
KJV renders: × lie.

H7904.strongs:
