Meaning: literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning
KJV renders: (arise, be up, get (oneself) up, rise up) early (betimes), morning.

H7926.strongs:
Origin: from 7925;
Meaning: the neck (between the shoulders) as the place of burdens; figuratively, the spur of a hill
KJV renders: back, × consent, portion, shoulder.

H7927.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7926; ridge;
Meaning: Shekem, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shechem.

H7928.strongs:
Origin: for 7926;
Meaning: Shekem, the name of a Hivite and two Israelites
KJV renders: Shechem.

H7929.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 7926;
Meaning: the shoulderbone
KJV renders: shoulder blade.

H7930.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 7928;
Meaning: a Shikmite (collectively), or descendants of Shekem
KJV renders: Shichemites.

H7931.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (apparently akin (by transmission) to 7901 through the idea of lodging; compare 5531, 7925);
Meaning: to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: abide, continue, (cause to, make to) dwell(-er), have habitation, inhabit, lay, place, (cause to) remain, rest, set (up).

H7933.strongs:
Origin: from 7931;
Meaning: a residence
KJV renders: habitation.

H7934.strongs:
Origin: from 7931;
Meaning: a resident; by extension, a fellow-citizen
KJV renders: inhabitant, neighbour, nigh.

H7935.strongs:
Origin: or (prolonged) שְׁכַנְיָהוּ; from 7931 and 3050; Jah has dwelt;
Meaning: Shekanjah, the name of nine Israelites
KJV renders: Shecaniah, Shechaniah.

H7936.strongs:
Origin: or (by permutation) סָכַר; (Ezra 4:5), a primitive root (apparently akin (by prosthesis) to 3739 through the idea of temporary purchase; compare 7937);
Meaning: to hire
KJV renders: earn wages, hire (out self), reward, × surely.

H7937.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
